
# Learning Notes – Sprint 28

## Overview

Sprint 28 focused on creating a Student Profile Form using Lightning Web Components and Lightning Data Service in the Student Placement Portal.

## Concepts Learned

- Learned how to create a Student Profile LWC.
- Understood how to identify the current student's Salesforce record.
- Learned how to create a Lookup relationship between `Student__c` and `User`.
- Understood how Lightning Data Service can be used to read and update Salesforce records.
- Learned how to use Lightning base components for form fields.
- Learned how to handle successful form submission.
- Learned how to handle form errors.
- Understood how to add an LWC to an existing Lightning App Builder page.
- Learned how to update Salesforce records through a Lightning form.

## Key Takeaways

- Lightning Data Service can simplify record access and updates.
- A Lookup(User) relationship can connect a Student record with a Salesforce User.
- Lightning base components provide standard Salesforce form behaviour.
- Success and error messages improve the user experience.
- A component can be added to an existing Lightning App Builder page without creating a separate page.
- Sprint 28 added profile management functionality to the Student Placement Portal.
